A substitute with indicatory ङ् replaces only the final letter, even if it has multiple letters.

This excepts @ref[1.1.55] (which says multi-letter substitutes replace the whole word).

**Example:** By @ref[6.3.25], आनङ् replaces ॠ-final words in dvandva compounds. Being ङित्, it replaces only the final:
मातृ + पितृ → माता + पितृ → मातापितरौ "mother and father"

@note[type=exception]{The substitute तातङ् (@ref[7.1.35]) replaces the whole word despite being ङित्: जीवतु → जीवतात् "may he live."}
